task_clean.explanation:
Demonstrated bypass using only solver-accessible files in the default shared verifier mode (task.toml specifies no separate mode). I wrote /app/auth_server_fixed.c containing '#include <unistd.h>
/* enc_len + 1 */
int main(int argc,char **argv){execv("/app/auth_server",argv);return 1;}'. This delegates every operation to the original vulnerable binary and fixes no memory corruption. Running the complete tests/test_outputs.py with the pytest dependencies and CTRF options from tests/test.sh produced 7 passed; applying test.sh's exit-status reward rule produced reward 1. The original binary is explicitly supplied to the solver, and the exploit neither reads review-only files at runtime nor alters tests. test_buffer_fix_present accepts the comment because it only searches for 'enc_len + 1'; behavioral comparisons naturally pass when executing the original. Consequently passing does not demonstrate the central requirement to fix all memory safety vulnerabilities. Additional defects: this source-pattern assertion can reject valid safe implementations using static buffers, and the size test uses zlib compression with a <1300 threshold instead of the instructed gzip size <1200. Inspected all task files, including tests/setup.sh; no setup_files or reference solution files are present. Nothing under /app/task-under-review was modified.

